<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑβρ-ιστικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>given to wantonness, insolent, outrageous,</i> of
			persons, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				396b
			</span></i>, etc.; of words, acts, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					252b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. καὶ βάρβαρος ἐπιστολή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.238
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. διάθεσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1385b31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. ἀδικήματα</span>
			<i>such as proceed from wanton insolence,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1391a19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑβριστικὰ καὶ μανικὰ λέγοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					307b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παθὼν ὑ. καὶ δεινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					45.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὃ καὶ -κώτατον συμβέβηκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					17.23
				</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>”
				<i>an insolent disposition,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					3.10.5
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ Ὑ.,</span> name of a festival
			at Argos, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.245e
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Chrm.</u>
					175d
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.1.33
			</span></i> (v.l.), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς διακεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					53.3
				</span></i>
			: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					22.54
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., of
			vines, <i>wanton, luxuriant,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.15.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>relating to an outrage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διήγησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Dem.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
